{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790262109,"nonce":"q2rD3XHmODXSKlstzVD6nOvPgYI=","title":"No verb starts a new game","message":"**The gap**\nNothing in the protocol starts a colony. openrun-20260909 counted it as intervention #1 (LEDGER D1): the Nepo scenario needed a fresh colony, \"none of the 139 verbs can start a new game\", and Dorian had to click New Colony -\u003e Nepo from the menu. Every fresh-colony run and every rwtest scenario that wants a clean map pays the same cost.\n\n**Prior art (found 2026-09-24, comparing against zorrobyte/rimbridge)**\nRimBridge ships `game.new_game {scenario, storyteller, difficulty, seed, map_size, permadeath}`. It stores the request, disposes the current game, and queues the Play scene with `Current.Game == null`. `Root_Play.Start` then takes the quicktest path. A Harmony prefix on `Root_Play.SetupForQuickTestPlay` sees the pending request and runs a parameterised setup in place of the dev quicktest (rimbridge `Source/Game/GameControl.cs`).\n\n**The catch in this repo**\nMain-thread verbs drain from `AgentGameComponent.GameComponentUpdate`. At the main menu there is no Game, so they answer `no-active-game`. A verb that starts a game from the menu needs a drain that runs with no game: RimBridge drains from a `Root.Update` postfix. Verify it against the decompiled `Root.Update` / `Root_Play.Start` before copying it. The same drain is what `load` (50df87a) needs. It also has to live with `autostart.rws` ([[quicktest-and-autostart-collide]]), because the quicktest path is the one autostart hijacks.\n\n**Acceptance**\n- `new-game {scenario, storyteller, difficulty, seed?}` works from a running colony AND from the main menu. It returns once the new map is playable, with the new sid and tick. `status` is `ok` afterwards.\n- An unknown scenario, storyteller or difficulty is refused before the current game is disposed, and the refusal lists the known defNames.\n- A new colony on the Nepo scenario activates `NepoScenario.Active`. This is the D1 case.\n- The journal shows a game boundary between the two sessions. `RefusalStreak` and the read watermark reset the way they do at any other boundary.\n- A parked or present `Saves/autostart.rws` does not hijack the new game. If it would, the verb refuses and names the file.","files":null}]}